From e8d70c6409b3c06bfc7f1d5eb7469bfd88dbb115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:32:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): keep a collapsed paste's payload when a submit is
 queued or busy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A collapsed paste lives in the composer's tokens, and `clearIn()` drops
those tokens synchronously on submit. The idle path expands the paste
before that happens. The busy path (`handleBusyInput(queueItem(full))`)
and the no-session path (`enqueue(full)`) instead keep the display string
with the `[[ … ]]` label and try to expand it later against tokens that
are already gone. In every busy_input_mode (interrupt, steer, queue), and
for input typed before the first session exists, the model gets the
literal label and the pasted body is lost (#99032).

The queue drain also judged `!` and `{!...}` by `item.text`. For a /queue
item, that is the expanded paste. So a paste whose content starts with `!`
was shell-executed when it drained, and `{!...}` inside a paste was
interpolated.

- Busy and no-session submits queue the expanded text, keep the label as
  `display`, and carry their own paste expander, because the composer
  tokens no longer exist when the item drains.
- `sendQueued` takes the whole QueueItem. It gates `!` and `{!...}` on
  `display`, interpolates the display, and then expands the paste into
  the result. That is the same split the direct submit path already uses.
  The model gets the payload, and the transcript keeps the label.
- `dequeue()` returns the QueueItem. Double-Enter and Ctrl+K now drain
  through `sendQueued`, like the idle drain effect, instead of
  re-dispatching the text as if it were fresh composer input.
- The interrupt path passes `display` to `send`, so the user bubble keeps
  the label.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
